# Coding Rules

- Do not use `any`.
- Validate user input.
- Keep secrets server-side.
- Never expose service-role keys.
- Use semantic HTML.
- Maintain responsive mobile-first layouts.
- Use reusable components.
- Include loading, empty, and error states.
- Do not create placeholder features that pretend to work.
- Do not modify brand logo artwork.
- Do not implement all features in one task.

# Safety

- Anonymous does not mean unaccountable.
- Report, block, and end-room controls must remain accessible.
- Contact reveal requires consent from both users.
- Do not expose email, Telegram ID, phone, or social handles publicly.
